  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed two storey side extension by reason of its combined siting, height and depth would result in a visually intrusive, dominant and overbearing form of development to the detriment of the residential amenity of nearby occupants.  The proposals would be contrary to London Plan policy D3 and policies D12.3 and D12.4 of the Merton Local Plan (2024).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed two storey side extension, by reason of the combined siting, design, bulk and massing, represents a visually intrusive and dominant form of development that would detract from the appearance, scale and proportions of the host dwelling, failing to relate positively and appropriately to the siting, scale, proportions and massing of surrounding buildings, existing street patterns and the existing suburban character and sense of openness at the location and as such would be harmful to the visual amenities of the Allgood Close streetscene and neighbouring occupiers. The proposals would be contrary to London Plan policy D3 and policies D12.3 and D12.4 of the Merton Local Plan (2024).",
    "Reason : 3 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required substantial changes such that a new application would be required. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
